{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794791545,"nonce":"W310AHcPEtA/HSD7lt6dT6v5jAU=","title":"No way to blur the desktop behind a window (Mica, Apple vibrancy, KDE blur); Material::Glass only blurs what Blinc draws itself","message":"Two visual styles we rebuild ask for a translucent window over a blurred desktop: Windows 11 (Mica/Acrylic) and macOS (vibrancy of sidebars). Blinc has `Material::Glass`, and it works: offscreen, black and white 10 px stripes behind a `GlassMaterial::new().blur(20).tint(..).saturation(1.8)` panel: the largest step between neighbouring pixels is 255 outside and 23 under the panel. But it blurs only what Blinc has drawn in the same window.\n\n`WindowConfig::transparent` exists. A search of blinc_platform and blinc_platform_desktop (blur, backdrop, acrylic, vibrancy, wallpaper, mica) finds no way to ask the compositor for a blur behind the window (KDE `org_kde_kwin_blur`, Windows `DWMWA_SYSTEMBACKDROP_TYPE`, macOS `NSVisualEffectView`), and none to read the wallpaper colour.\n\nWanted: a window option for the system backdrop (none, blur, mica) per platform, `Unsupported` where the platform has none. Until then our styles draw the flat tint of the material (`fs-components-styles`, `Surface::Backdrop`).","files":null}]}